    {
        "content": "<p>This is isomorphic to the <a href=\"#narrow/channel/428973-nightly-testing/topic/lean.2313363.2C.20more.20transparency.20bump.20issues\">post about lean#13363</a>, but for <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/13492\">lean#13492</a>.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>feat: stricter @[defeq] inference <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/13492\">lean#13492</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>adds a stricter check on whether a <code>:= rfl</code> theorem gets <code>@[defeq]</code>, tightening up when definitional equalities are used during simp / elaboration.</p>\n<p>The bulk of the mathlib adaptation is just <code>set_option backward.defeqAttrib.useBackward true</code> applied file- or declaration-locally (roughly 1060 files), which is noisy but mechanical. There are, however, a handful of proofs on the <code>lean-pr-testing-13492</code> branch which needed ad hoc <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4-nightly-testing/compare/nightly-testing...lean-pr-testing-13492\">fixes</a> beyond the <code>set_option</code> escape hatch. Some of the fixes are fine, but some are not great, and should just be considered as emergency patches. I've labelled all of these clearly with <code>#adaptation_note</code>s.</p>\n<p>Could I ask for some assistance properly repairing these proofs? The goal is to either:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>decide the new proof is okay, and just remove the <code>#adaptation_note</code></li>\n<li>write a new proof (possibly changing the earlier API and adding simp lemmas to avoid the defeq problem that is now breaking the old proof)</li>\n<li>or complain that this is a severe problem, and you think it warrants further attention on the lean4 side.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Currently, the fixes are only on the <code>lean-pr-testing-13492</code> branch on the mathlib4-nightly-testing fork. You can either make a PR to that branch, send me a diff, push changes directly if you have write access, or ask me to add you to the nightly-testing Github team so that you have write access! (If you're confident pushing directly, please please do so, we'll have a chance to review this in the <code>bump/</code> process.)</p>\n<p>Later these fixes will arrive in Mathlib master (not certain yet whether this will be via an RC in the v4.30 series, or in v4.31.0-rc1), and I'll probably ping more widely for help at that stage for any remaining <code>#adaptation_note</code>s.</p>",
        "id": 590602292,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1776995552
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm now going to ping relevant people (the Authors list + recent committers) for the affected files. Sorry for the noise, of course helping here is not compulsory, and these problems can just join the technical debt backlog. :-)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>edit: fixed <del><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4-nightly-testing/blob/lean-pr-testing-13492/Mathlib/Algebra/Homology/DerivedCategory/Ext/Map.lean#L67\"><code>Algebra/Homology/DerivedCategory/Ext/Map</code></a> — <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"749361\">@Nailin Guan</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"750070\">@Wang Jingting</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"479299\">@Jovan Gerbscheid</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"634338\">@Michael Rothgang</span></del></li>\n<li>edit: fixed <del><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4-nightly-testing/blob/lean-pr-testing-13492/Mathlib/AlgebraicTopology/ExtraDegeneracy.lean#L101\"><code>AlgebraicTopology/ExtraDegeneracy</code></a> — <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"459699\">@Joël Riou</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"519559\">@Dagur Asgeirsson</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"308587\">@Li Xuanji</span></del></li>\n<li>edit: fixed <del><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4-nightly-testing/blob/lean-pr-testing-13492/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/FilteredColimitCommutesFiniteLimit.lean#L93\"><code>CategoryTheory/Limits/FilteredColimitCommutesFiniteLimit</code></a> — <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"519559\">@Dagur Asgeirsson</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"479299\">@Jovan Gerbscheid</span></del></li>\n<li>edit: fixed <del><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4-nightly-testing/blob/lean-pr-testing-13492/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Sites/Descent/IsPrestack.lean#L107\"><code>CategoryTheory/Sites/Descent/IsPrestack</code></a> — <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"459699\">@Joël Riou</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"648495\">@Christian Merten</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"519559\">@Dagur Asgeirsson</span></del></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4-nightly-testing/blob/lean-pr-testing-13492/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Determinant.lean#L148\"><code>LinearAlgebra/Determinant</code></a> — <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110294\">@Johannes Hölzl</span>, <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"210574\">Patrick Massot</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"198529\">@Casper Putz</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"238446\">@Anne Baanen</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"634338\">@Michael Rothgang</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4-nightly-testing/blob/lean-pr-testing-13492/Mathlib/Order/JordanHolder.lean#L288\"><code>Order/JordanHolder</code></a> — <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110044\">@Chris Hughes</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"330967\">@Wrenna Robson</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"767479\">@Harald Husum</span></li>\n<li>edit: fixed <del><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4-nightly-testing/blob/lean-pr-testing-13492/Mathlib/Order/OmegaCompletePartialOrder.lean#L745\"><code>Order/OmegaCompletePartialOrder</code></a> — <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110026\">@Simon Hudon</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"571277\">@Ira Fesefeldt</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"238446\">@Anne Baanen</span>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"421885\">@Joscha Mennicken</span></del></li>\n</ul>",
