    },
    {
        "content": "<p>From the PR description</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>@[defeq]</code> is now inferred only when the equation holds at <code>.instances</code> transparency</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If I understand this correctly this means that</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst_foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>no longer creates a dsimp lemma?</p>\n<p>If so, I think this breaks an extremely common use of <code>dsimp</code>, which is to unfold bundled morphisms by rewriting along <code>fooHom x = foo x</code>.</p>",
        "id": 590638068,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1777014710
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If my understanding is correct, then I'd perhaps argue that <code>simps</code> should add <code>defeq</code> attributes automatically</p>",
        "id": 590638381,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1777014822
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, it looks like this might be massively breaking our reliance on <code>dsimp</code> in category theory.</p>",
        "id": 590639116,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1777015067
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>May I ask why this change to inference of <code>@[defeq]</code> is planned? What lemmas should not be tagged with <code>@[defeq]</code> that are tagged with the old algorithm?</p>",
        "id": 590677602,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1777026551
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>May I ask why this change to inference of <code>@[defeq]</code> is planned? What lemmas should not be tagged with <code>@[defeq]</code> that are tagged with the old algorithm?</p>",
        "id": 590677635,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1777026562
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/428973-nightly-testing/topic/lean.2313492.2C.20stricter.20.40.5Bdefeq.5D.20inference/near/590638381\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If my understanding is correct, then I'd perhaps argue that <code>simps</code> should add <code>defeq</code> attributes automatically</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Note that the adaption branch also has changes to some of mathlib’s meta code (setting some option or the other), that you probably want to treat as an adaption-todo. This may hide some more widespread breakage.</p>",
        "id": 590701308,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1777033440
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"648495\">Christian Merten</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/428973-nightly-testing/topic/lean.2313492.2C.20stricter.20.40.5Bdefeq.5D.20inference/near/590677635\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>May I ask why this change to inference of <code>@[defeq]</code> is planned? What lemmas should not be tagged with <code>@[defeq]</code> that are tagged with the old algorithm?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Lemmas that do not hold at <code>instance</code> tranparency.</p>\n<p>My understanding is (correct me if I am wrong, Kim): The goal is that proof goals are type correct at instance transparency. <code>dsimp</code> rewrites in positions that are dependent on elsewhere. Therefore, dsimp may only do rewrites that are valid at instance transparency.</p>\n<p>This PR does not do that yet, but in a follow up we plan to apply the same discipline to <code>:= rfl</code> lemmas and theorems explicitly marked as <code>@[defeq]</code>. </p>\n<p>One “fix” is to make more definitions <code>implicit_reducible</code>. I cannot offer guidance when that’s the best way forward.</p>",
        "id": 590702005,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1777033617
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"286014\">Robin Carlier</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/428973-nightly-testing/topic/lean.2313492.2C.20stricter.20.40.5Bdefeq.5D.20inference/near/590639116\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yes, it looks like this might be massively breaking our reliance on <code>dsimp</code> in category theory.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Maybe category theory should consider using the <code>implicit_reducible</code> tag more liberally?</p>",
        "id": 590867863,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1777120281
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That’s also how I’m starting to understand things. I’ll be trying to experiment with some annotations over the course of next week.</p>",
        "id": 590869665,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1777121771
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm also starting to wonder if basic things like <code>Function.comp</code> and <code>Function.id</code> should be tagged <code>implicit_reducible</code>.</p>",
        "id": 590869742,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1777121867
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I’m planning to merge this after another round of update-to-<code>nightly-with-mathlib</code>-and-fixing-the-adaption branch</p>",
        "id": 591044709,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1777268037
